  "question": {
    "text": "As shown in the figure, a plane mirror is fixed at a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the bottom of tank containing water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. The height of water in the tank is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. A small bulb is placed at the bottom of the water tank. The distance of image of the bulb formed by mirror from the bottom of the tank is&nbsp; ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0070_42b35808ec8c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 191px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "98",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The data given is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Apparent depth is</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math><br />Distance of object from mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br />Distance of image from bottom of tank <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>98</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
  }
